                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Diagnose the intellectual-capital gaps`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `Sendoa is <strong>rich in knowledge but failing to mobilize it</strong>. New-product revenue has fallen from 38% to 19%; engineers in different units solve the same problems twice; and three senior architects left with undocumented design patterns. Diagnose the binding constraint across the three components of intellectual capital — <strong>human</strong> (skills, departures), <strong>structural</strong> (no documentation, siloed systems) and <strong>relational</strong> (external co-innovation). The trap: treating this as a pure hiring problem and refilling roles while the structural leak — nothing documented, units siloed — stays open. And weight <em>urgency</em>: two more architects can retire in 18 months, taking ~€2.1M of tacit knowledge with them.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Plan: choose where to invest the €5M`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `Allocate the <strong>€5 million</strong> across five knowledge-sharing mechanisms: expert-capture / apprenticeship (€0.9M, the most urgent — retirements), platform relaunch + curation (€1.4M), communities of practice (€0.6M), cross-unit rotation (€0.8M) and open innovation (€1.2M). The full menu is ~€4.9M, so you must <strong>prioritize</strong>. Resist the instinct to fund a little of everything — spread thinly and no programme reaches the adoption threshold that creates impact. <em>Adoption, not purchase, is what failed in 2021.</em> Concentrate on the urgent and the high-impact.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Decide: set incentives so tacit knowledge flows`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Mechanisms without incentives die — the 2021 platform proved it. Engineers are rewarded for shipping their own unit's features, not for sharing or reusing. Redesign the <strong>incentive and governance system</strong>: how heavily sharing weighs in bonus and promotion, what behaviour you actually reward (reuse and impact, or vanity activity), and whether you fund protected time and curation ownership. The tension: reward sharing too little and nothing flows; reward it too much and engineers <em>write wikis instead of shipping product</em>. Find the balance — and gate it on innovation outcomes, not raw volume.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Recover & commit: convert knowledge into output`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Build the one-year roadmap that lifts new-product revenue back toward 30%. But a <em>mid-year shock</em> hits: platform adoption is lagging and a senior architect has just announced early retirement, with €1.0M still uncommitted. Decide whether to redirect funds and accelerate expert-capture before the knowledge walks. Then choose what goes on the board's dashboard — <strong>innovation outcomes</strong> (new-idea rate, time-to-innovation, new-product revenue) or vanity <strong>activity</strong> (1,200 posts, 60 café sessions). The board will press: is this real innovation, or knowledge theatre?`,

                    r1_constraint_label:    `Which intellectual-capital component is Sendoa's binding constraint right now?`,
                    r1_urgency_label:       `What is the most urgent, irreversible risk to weight first?`,
                    r1_rigour_label:        `How rigorously does your team map the gaps by impact AND urgency, not just gut feel? (%)`,
                    r1_rigour_readout:      `Diagnostic rigour (impact × urgency mapping):`,
                    con_human:              `Human + structural capital together — departed architects AND nothing documented, units siloed`,
                    con_hiring:             `Purely human capital — just replace the lost architects with senior hires`,
                    con_relational:         `Purely relational capital — weak co-innovation with customers and universities`,
                    con_even:               `All three are equally weak — fix everything at once`,
                    urg_tacit:              `Tacit knowledge walking out — two architects can retire in 18 months, undocumented`,
                    urg_platform:           `The unused 2021 platform — relaunch it as the priority`,
                    urg_revenue:            `The revenue number itself — chase short-term sales, worry about knowledge later`,
                    urg_none:               `Nothing is truly urgent — take the full year to study the problem`,

